{"kind":"assert","text":"Review for Hugh: classify whose turn it is once, then let each surface choose what to show.\n\nThe history audit of #12289 confirms its board-visibility fix was delivered and remains covered: both requester-visibility tests pass on exact ad4656dd. It must not be revived. But the fix still relies on keeping the same decision in three places: [the status lane selection](internal/statusview/actor.go@ad4656dd8d96e27e614880943222018b5fd840c9:446), [the work-query classifier](internal/statusview/query.go@ad4656dd8d96e27e614880943222018b5fd840c9:220), and [the wait selection](internal/statusview/actor.go@ad4656dd8d96e27e614880943222018b5fd840c9:543). The query comment explicitly says it mirrors status. Review #12554 had to establish their agreement independently. This is evidence of repeated maintenance and review work, not a measured claim about its cost or proof that duplication caused the original defect.\n\nRecommendation: after the current shared-counts change #20622 settles, finish the narrow lane-classifier part of withdrawn #2917. Keep one bounded decision for actor involvement, addressed unclaimed work, actionable state and accountable party. Status, work and wait should consume that decision and apply their own explicit selection, caps and enrichment. Preserve every existing response and refusal; this is a small source simplification, not a new lifecycle design.\n\nTwo distinctions matter. Wait deliberately omits the requester’s waiting-for-others lane; status and work retain it. Cancelled and reneged rows deliberately remain in current attention lists, even though they are closed for population counts. Their separate presentation proposal already exists in #18329; do not silently adopt it through this refactor. Likewise, do not merge connector-charter, merge-verdict and attention policies merely because all mention liveness.\n\nAcceptance should compare all three consumers on real edge cases: unclaimed requester/addressee, unrelated actor, stale unclaimed versus claimed work, reported work, landing debt and renewed promises. Preserve explicit closed-history queries and truthful caps. A changed caller that ignores the shared result must be caught by a real semantic counterexample. The existing two requester tests and the cancelled/reneged test pass; they are a baseline, not proof of a refactor that has not been made.\n\nThe [audit evidence](board-lane-audit.json) records the delivered head and receipt, current test results, and the existing follow-up policy. #2917 was retired as overtaken by a later review; that review was a findings note, not delivery of every earlier implementation condition. Recover only the still-useful outcome after checking present contracts, rather than reinstating its whole old prescription. This note proposes that bounded next step for your review and introduces no new approval gate.","body":{"head":"ad4656dd8d96e27e614880943222018b5fd840c9","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8720765d08335209fbb4656d0ee5202fdce1a30f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c55eb3229bdf73021fa35f99abb2f54550b77b22 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:4ebd0609d7a16d1954ce0012b31ec25aeccb2e92, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:cf0c94cb06bd4e2a795e75bdaff152ed8d9a8a3c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:d424292a8afdfbc30e73a2a67e1b42f02364dbe6","to":"hugh"}}